    {
      "color": "6",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "ddbffbf3a4fd1e43",
      "text": "---\ncssclasses: cc-border-left, cc-border-right, cc-border-dashed\n---\n\n# Lesson 3: Try decorating a card for yourself",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 680,
      "x": -520,
      "y": -40
    },
    {
      "height": 340,
      "id": "49991612edd60567",
      "text": "---\ncssclasses: cc-border-none, cc-card-transparent\n---\n\nIt is now your turn to try making a decorated card using a ccsclass command provided by Canvas Candy. Follow these steps:\n\n1. Double-click the card below to put it into edit mode\n2. on the first line type three dashes `---`. You'll notice that a blank line is added, then another line with three dashes `---`. Obsidian is preparing the editor for you to add properties, in our case the `cssclasses` property.\n3. type in `cssclasses: cc-border-double` \n6. Now go to the fourth line, which should be empty. Type some text into the card, like HELLO WORLD\n7. Now click outside the card to see the decoration take affect.",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 680,
      "x": -520,
      "y": 40
    },
    {
      "color": "5",
      "height": 167,
      "id": "0b91d3be37577a8f",
      "text": "",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 240,
      "x": -460,
      "y": 380
    },
    {
      "color": "5",
      "height": 167,
      "id": "826b90187feb47ab",
      "text": "---\ncssclasses: cc-border-double\n---\n",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 240,
      "x": -110,
      "y": 464
    },
    {
      "height": 60,
      "id": "40398b2bfb24b07f",
      "text": "---\ncssclasses: cc-border-none, cc-card-transparent\n---\n\nThe card should now look similar to this card:",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 250,
      "x": -120,
      "y": 380
    },
    {
      "height": 60,
      "id": "ed1b79bfe374b327",
      "text": "---\ncssclasses: cc-border-rounded,  cc-border-right, cc-card-center, cc-card-gradient-0deg\n---\n\n[[Lesson 04 - Using multiple decorations in a card.canvas|Next]]",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 140,
